# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore rules for the MUSA app-service repository.
# Principle: anything large, derived or machine-specific stays on disk only.
# git never forgets a binary, so the decision has to be made before the add.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Derived / tooling state ---------------------------------------------
# Codebase Memory MCP local index; rebuildable with index_repository.
.codebase-memory/

# --- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
build/
_build/

# --- Scratch / pre-selection material -------------------------------------
# Downloads, shortlists and dead ends, e.g. the marketing image pre-selection
# in scratch/marketing_images/. Nothing under scratch/ is referenced by
# source/, so it must not pad every clone.
scratch/

# --- Local editor / agent configuration -----------------------------------
# Deliberately TRACKED, not ignored. .claude/, .cursor/, .vscode/ and .zed/
# hold this project's agent rules and MCP setup, which the team needs; ignoring
# them would also silently skip NEW files placed in those folders.
# Caveat: the MCP configs embed a machine-specific absolute path such as
# c:\Users\<user>\...\codebase-memory-mcp.exe, so a collaborator may have to
# adjust theirs. If that becomes a real problem, version a .dist template
# instead of ignoring the folder.

# --- 3D models kept out of git on purpose ---------------------------------
# ~26 MB of GLB. Three of the four are the Khronos glTF Sample Assets and are
# reproduced byte-for-byte by tools/fetch_models.py; the fourth is a manual
# download. Binary payloads belong in a CDN or an object store, not in the
# history of a code repository.
*.glb

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ---------------------------------------------
# .git/    Not a worktree path: it IS the repository. Git never tracks paths
#          inside .git/, so a rule here is a no-op. Its size is HISTORY, and
#          history only shrinks by rewriting it or by keeping big binaries out
#          in the first place -- which is what the *.glb rule above is for.
# .github/ Holds the CI workflows and .github/copilot-instructions.md. GitHub
#          reads those from the REMOTE, so ignoring them would silently break
#          CI and strip the project agent rules from every collaborator.

# --- OS artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
